peterb@telerama.lm.com (Pete Berger) writes:
>I am trying to compile nethack 3.1.3 for MSDOS using DJGPP 1.11, gnu
>cc v. 2.5.7.  Unfortunately, it keeps telling me that there are
>inconsistent declarations of "exit" -- std.h for GCC, and in various
>files from nethack.  Has anyone else had this problem, and how did
>they fix it?

Not being a C guru, but having a *bit* of experience in this, my suggestions
are:

a) change the type-declarations of "exit" in the nethack files to match
that of std.h

or

b) copy std.h to the make directory, replace all occurrences of
#include <std.h>
by
#include "std.h"
and edit the type-declaration of "exit" in the local copy of std.h to match
that in Nethack

or

c) see if simply commenting out the #include <std.h> line lets it compile...

